--- body ---

## Context

Task recall searches beyond the resident cut. Integrate existing .knowledge.toml pointers/caveats without turning domain assets, reusable code or decision registers into memory bodies.

Design baseline: v6, merged by PR #903. See `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md` and `docs/2026-09-11-memory-implementation-plan.md`. This planning change implements nothing and closes no work.

## Relevant files

Library/CLI; `rules/knowledge-hints.md`; `scripts/knowledge_hints.py`; pilot corpus and available shared snapshot.

## Actions

1. Search title, description, tags and body with a simple lexical baseline; use explicit applicability for exclusion, not missing keywords.
2. Select a bounded task bundle with provenance, status and caveats; adjust redundancy here without permanently penalising particulars in static orientation.
3. Reuse pointer/caveat discovery and deduplicate canonical artefacts; account knowledge-hint exposure separately from controlled memory.
4. Expose explicit historical retrieval with inactive status and replacement links; ordinary recall always excludes those records and redirects.
5. Use the validated current-corpus fallback from 0921 when ranking/publication is absent or corrupt; lexical recall must not depend on a healthy dream snapshot. Return empty or incomplete results honestly; expose uncached shared coverage. No embeddings or hosted backend required.

## Test

Fixtures retrieve a below-cut lesson, preserve a local exception beside a generalisation, exclude inactive advice, return no advice for irrelevant input, and exercise simultaneous hint/memory references with no duplicate pointer or lost caveat.

## Verification

- [ ] Run the focused fixtures and show they detect the relevant failure.
- [ ] Run applicable repository checks; record commands, results and limitations.
- [ ] Confirm the implementation matches this scope and v6, including explicit capability limits.

## Invariants

- Canonical bodies and provenance remain reviewable; memory cannot override decisions.
- No mandatory residency, automatic generalisation, new native-memory modes or policy duplication.
- Use the common library and normal Git integration; no runtime implementation is part of the planning PR.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Task bundle bounded and provenance-preserving; all available eligible sources searched.
- [ ] Existing knowledge assets keep their canonical ownership.
- [ ] Offline lexical path is sufficient for the first adapter.
